+\&\fBsize\fR resembles output from System V \fBsize\fR (using \fB\-A\fR,
+or \fB\-\-format=sysv\fR), or Berkeley \fBsize\fR (using \fB\-B\fR, or
+\&\fB\-\-format=berkeley\fR).  The default is the one\-line format similar to
+Berkeley\*(Aqs.  Alternatively, you can choose the GNU format output
+(using \fB\-G\fR, or \fB\-\-format=gnu\fR), this is similar to
+Berkeley\*(Aqs output format, but sizes are counted differently.
+.Sp
+Here is an example of the Berkeley (default) format of output from
+\&\fBsize\fR:
+.Sp
+.Vb 4
+\&        $ size \-\-format=Berkeley ranlib size
+\&           text    data     bss     dec     hex filename
+\&         294880   81920   11592  388392   5ed28 ranlib
